      en: "Tohua Kamuihei is a traditional Polynesian meeting place on Nuku Hiva Island. It served as a venue for dances, festivals, and political assemblies. The complex consists of a large rectangular platform surrounded by stone seating rows. Tohua Kamuihei was built in the 19th century and reflects the social organization of the Marquesas Islands. Today, it is an important cultural heritage site and is used for traditional events. Archaeological work has uncovered and restored the structure.",
