      en: "St. Michael's Cathedral in Rikitea on Mangareva Island is one of the oldest churches in French Polynesia. It was built in 1838 by French missionaries and dedicated to the Archangel Michael. The church is constructed from coral blocks bonded with lime mortar. The interior features wood carvings and colorful stained glass windows. The cathedral served as the center of Catholic mission in the Gambier Islands. It is an architectural gem showing a blend of European and Polynesian styles.",
