      en: "The Paeke archaeological site on Nuku Hiva Island is one of the most significant in the Marquesas. It includes residential platforms, marae, and burial sites dating from the 10th to 18th centuries. Findings demonstrate dense population and complex social organization. Stone statues (Tiki) are scattered across the site. The site was scientifically studied in the 20th century. Paeke provides comprehensive insight into pre-colonial life in the Marquesas, including craftsmanship and trade relations. It is a protected cultural heritage.",
