      en: "Marae Tehoro on Tahiti is a significant archaeological site that served as a political and ceremonial center for indigenous Polynesians. Built from basalt and coral stones, the platform showcases the advanced construction techniques of Polynesian architects. Used between the 14th and 18th centuries, it was the venue for sacrifices and assemblies. Today it is a protected cultural heritage site, offering insights into pre-colonial social structures. Located near the coast amidst lush vegetation, it is maintained by local guides.",
