      en: "Marae Hauviri in Opoa, Raiatea, is a significant marae considered the birthplace of Polynesian civilization. Built in the 13th century, it is the oldest known marae in the Society Islands. The platform is massive, built from basalt blocks and decorated with carved animals. Here the god 'Oro was worshipped, and priests consecrated new chiefs. The marae was a center of cult and navigation. After European contact, it fell into disrepair. Excavated in the 1990s, it is now a UNESCO World Heritage candidate.",
